          "title": "You'll want to know: calda, caldae",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "calda, caldae — \"hot water (for mixing with wine)\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Hospes caldam et vīnum rogat. The guest asks for hot water and wine."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "First declension, feminine: calda, caldae f., short for (aqua) calida. Romans liked wine mixed with hot water in winter."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "calda is a shortened form of (aqua) calida 'hot water', from calidus 'hot' (Lewis & Short), which is built on caleō 'to be warm'."
            }
          ]
        },
