              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "fūmōsus, fūmōsa, fūmōsum — \"smoky, full of smoke\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Popīna fūmōsa est, et oculī hospitum dolent. The cookshop is smoky, and the customers' eyes hurt."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "An adjective of three endings, from fūmus 'smoke' with -ōsus 'full of'. Poets mock the smoky tavern."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "fūmōsus is built on fūmus 'smoke' with the suffix -ōsus 'full of' (Lewis & Short). English fume comes from fūmus."
            }
          ]
        },
